Deliberate open-source carve-outs, which carry their own license terms:

- The host CLI (PocketShell-io/pocketshell-cli, PyPI package `pocketshell`)
  is MIT, and the bundled `aplexer` is Apache-2.0; both carry their own
  license files in their own repositories and are distributed separately
  from the app.
- Vendored Termux `terminal-emulator` / `terminal-view` code
  (shared/core-terminal): Apache-2.0, see
  shared/core-terminal/LICENSE.txt.
- JetBrainsMono-Regular.ttf: SIL Open Font License 1.1, see
  shared/core-terminal/src/main/assets/fonts/OFL.txt.
- All other third-party dependencies keep their upstream licenses; the
  notices shipped with the binary are collected in
  app2/src/main/res/raw/third_party_licenses.txt.

Charging for PocketShell changes none of this: the app is paid and closed,
the CLI and aux tooling stay free and open.
